# Python virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
# A worktree's own backend/.venv is often a symlink to the shared venv outside the repo — the
# trailing-slash patterns above only match a real directory, not a symlink, so this bare form
# catches that case too.
.venv

# Python bytecode / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Django
backend/db.sqlite3
# Timestamped copies taken before a migration or a merge. Untracked but not ignored until
# now, so a stray `git add -A` staged several megabytes of database.
backend/db.sqlite3.bak-*
backend/media/
backend/staticfiles/

# Env files (frontend/.gitignore already covers frontend/.env*, this catches any elsewhere)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.test

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Redundant local backup archives (snapshots of dirs already tracked/vendored here)
/Archive.zip
/Database-of-Student-Exercise.zip

# Database-of-Student-Exercise/content/ IS tracked (vendored below) — it's the source data
# backend/exercises/management/commands/import_legacy_corpus.py reads to populate the DB, and
# scripts/extract_mock_exercises.py reads the same path; without it, README's own setup steps
# don't work on a fresh clone. Only that repo's own static-site generator/build tooling (unused by
# EdMat) is excluded — see its own README.md for what each of these does.
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/build/
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/site/
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/docs/
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/generator/
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/tests/
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/build.py
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/pytest.ini
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/README.md
/Database-of-Student-Exercise/requirements.txt

# Activity-log shards (telemetry app). Real personal data under a retention policy —
# never in git, and backed up separately from the main database.
backend/logdata/

# Shared on-disk cache (config/settings.py's CACHES). Holds rate-limit counters and cached
# geocoding results — pure runtime state, regenerated on demand, never worth committing.
backend/cachedata/

# The webek4/edmat.net server rescue (2026-08-07). Holds the production DJANGO_SECRET_KEY, the
# TLS private key for edmat.net, live DRF API tokens, the unsanitised production database and
# Apache logs with real user IPs. Must NEVER be committed — this line exists so a stray
# `git add -A` cannot publish it.
FUW/

# deploy/fuw/pack.sh fallback output dir (default is FUW/, already ignored)
dist/

# FUW deploy scripts — private, kept local-only (backed up under FUW/script-backups/)
deploy/fuw/

# The ING grant kit — deck, form answers, budget figures, the foundation paperwork. It is its own
# git repository (`grant/.git`) with its own private remote, so it has real version control while
# being structurally incapable of reaching this public repo. Untracked here on 2026-09-19; the
# history it had in THIS repo is preserved on the local branches `grant-kit-local` and
# `grant-history`. Never `git add -f` it back.
grant/
gemini.md

# Browser-check screenshots — looked at during a run, never part of the record.
# 48 of them had been sitting untracked for weeks; this stops the next commit sweeping them in.
frontend/e2e/screenshots/

# Claude Code's per-machine permission choices. Personal to one checkout, never part of the record.
.claude/settings.local.json

# run.sh output when it is run with the log redirected (run-local.log) — a local run, not a record.
run-local.log

# school-management-demo/ runtime output. The demo is a Node process with a JSON store: `npm start`,
# `npm test` and `npm run seed` write a whole school into data/ (names, grades, attendance and
# guardian contacts — synthetic, but shaped exactly like the real thing), `npm run smoke` drops a
# screenshot per screen into smoke-out/, and the retention job writes backup/. None of it is source.
school-management-demo/data/
school-management-demo/smoke-out/
school-management-demo/backup/
school-management-demo/backups/
